times: Standing in a group buys room to differ, up to a point, before the one who differs is asked to fall in line (idiosyncrasy credit: Hollander 1958)
gap: 3-8
scene: {N} has been part of {place} long enough to know everyone, and long enough for everyone to know that {N} does things differently. Today one of the regulars takes {N} aside. There have been remarks, she says, and it would be easier for everyone if {N} did things the way they are done here. She is not unkind about it. She would just like an answer.
scene W: {N} believes a group holds together on shared ways, and also that {Ns} own way is the fairer one.
scene U: {N} would change gladly if someone could say why. So far nobody has.
scene B: {N} weighs it coolly: a good name here is worth something, and so is being the one who does it differently.
scene R: {N} feels the heat rise. Being managed like this makes {N} want to walk out.
scene G: {N} thinks of the people back home who did it this way for years, and were loved for it.
